### 1\. First: Define exactly what we are building

I recommend dividing SeismoAI into three analytical systems.

Module 01

Historical Seismic Intelligence

Analyze historical earthquake events and discover patterns.

* Magnitude distribution.

* Earthquake frequency over time.

* Depth distribution.

* Geographic clustering.

* Seismic activity trends.

Module 02

Earthquake Probability Modeling

Estimate the probability of at least one earthquake above a defined magnitude threshold within a geographic region and future time window.

* Statistical baseline.

* Machine Learning classification.

* Regional probability estimates.

* Model confidence and calibration.

Module 03

Geospatial Risk Analysis

Analyze geographic distribution and identify areas with elevated historical seismic activity.

* Interactive earthquake maps.

* Seismic hotspots.

* Regional comparisons.

* Historical activity indicators.

Scientific limitation: We are not building a system that predicts the exact date, location, or magnitude of the next earthquake. Earthquake prediction of that kind is not scientifically reliable. We will estimate probabilities using historical observations and clearly communicate uncertainty.

